<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The browser trust line, 2026 ~ one custody context, no human counted

Four fresh reads of `K15` Wave B kept finding that other code on the same browser origin can erase an island's ledger, start a fresh empty one or take a session lock. A Copilot seat read the code and canon; a Codex Sol seat read the field; each traded and checked the other. Claims read MEASURED (read in code, canon or a cited source) or LEAD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! Findings

# ''The platform walls profiles, never one origin's contexts'' (both, MEASURED). `vessel-lock.ts` takes one Web Lock per store name on an origin and refuses `steal` in house code; MDN's Web Locks and SharedWorker pages state that any same-origin script may request, steal or reach them. Chrome's profile guidance states that anyone at the device's unlocked login may switch to any profile, so a profile walls storage and a locked OS account walls people.
# ''A hand names a session, never a person'' (both, MEASURED). `session-contract.mem` uses //hand// for every session actor (tab, CLI run, disk watcher, spirit seat); `persona-circle.mem` forbids a human constructor. "One profile, one vessel, one hand" holds as deployment guidance and never as a cardinality law the vessel tests.
# ''Today's per-face isolation runs as routing'' (Sol, MEASURED). The browser still seals rows under one vessel key until `K15` step 6's fence; the trust line reads honest once each face's secrets seal under its own key.
# ''Local absence proves nothing'' (Sol, MEASURED in MDN's storage-eviction guidance and `browser-vessel-identity.ts`). Origin storage can vanish whole, so a missing ledger cannot witness a clean history; peers adjudicate.
# ''Tiers map to relations'' (both, MEASURED in `cabal-realm.mem`, `identity-enacts-relation.mem`, `bounded-reach-contract.mem`, `kahu.mem`). Realms, charters and seats separate one operator's tiers; carriage carries and reads nothing; each power needs its own grant. Shared substrate correlates tiers by metadata (LEAD).

<<~/ahu>>

